We've met a thousand times.

519
00:54:32.302 --> 00:54:34.436
Now, why did you
really come back?

520
00:54:36.273 --> 00:54:38.139
- I love my son.

521
00:54:39.110 --> 00:54:40.860
I want to get better.

522
00:54:40.960 --> 00:54:44.346
I want my family back. Please.

523
00:54:45.382 --> 00:54:49.150
Please. Ahh! I swear!
I swear!

524
00:54:53.324 --> 00:54:54.673
I just want a chance--

525
00:54:54.773 --> 00:54:57.226
I just want a chance
at a relationship with my son.

526
00:54:57.827 --> 00:54:59.625
Hmm? As a father,
you gotta understand that.

527
00:54:59.724 --> 00:55:01.514
Please,
I'm begging you, please. I know.

528
00:55:01.614 --> 00:55:03.371
I know you think
I came back for the money.

529
00:55:03.471 --> 00:55:04.471
I didn't. I didn't know.

530
00:55:04.570 --> 00:55:05.967
- What money?

531
00:55:06.469 --> 00:55:08.070
- Chris didn't tell you?

532
00:55:08.905 --> 00:55:13.126
His mom, some uncle she hadn't
seen in years left her...

533
00:55:13.226 --> 00:55:17.079
I don't know, man,
I-- please, please, just...

534
00:55:19.449 --> 00:55:21.050
I don't know, man, please.

535
00:55:34.297 --> 00:55:36.231
I know guys like you.

536
00:55:39.637 --> 00:55:41.402
Prison's full of 'em.

537
00:55:42.706 --> 00:55:44.940
Monsters hiding in plain sight.

538
00:55:46.476 --> 00:55:48.911
You'll never really be
a father...

539
00:55:49.380 --> 00:55:51.012
or a husband.

540
00:55:52.148 --> 00:55:54.615
You'll never love anybody else
that much.

541
00:55:57.722 --> 00:56:00.773
What are you gonna do?
Hmm?

542
00:56:00.873 --> 00:56:02.108
What are you gonna do

543
00:56:02.208 --> 00:56:04.360
when they find out
who you really are?

544
00:56:06.864 --> 00:56:08.764
- Thank you for sharing.

545
00:56:44.001 --> 00:56:45.067
- Mom?

546
00:56:46.403 --> 00:56:49.054
- Hi, honey.
- What are you doing, Mom?

547
00:56:49.155 --> 00:56:51.340
<i>Just a bit of gardening,</i>
<i>honey.</i>

548
00:56:53.210 --> 00:56:54.327
- I saw you, Marie.

549
00:56:54.427 --> 00:56:55.784
- You're not taking him
anywhere.

550
00:56:55.885 --> 00:56:57.797
- I need you to come with me,
all right?

551
00:56:57.896 --> 00:57:00.367
I'm gonna take care of you now.
Doesn't that sound great?

552
00:57:00.467 --> 00:57:02.016
- You get the fuck away
from him.

553
00:57:03.586 --> 00:57:06.422
: <i>Come on, we gotta go.</i>

554
00:57:07.525 --> 00:57:08.690
Bitch!

555
00:57:17.701 --> 00:57:20.253
I am never gonna hurt you again,
I promise.

556
00:57:20.353 --> 00:57:21.969
Everything's gonna be okay.

557
00:57:50.934 --> 00:57:52.800
- You're a good boy, Evan.

558
00:57:53.603 --> 00:57:54.954
Mommy loves you,

559
00:57:55.054 --> 00:57:57.923
and I'm never gonna let
anything bad happen to you.

560
00:57:58.023 --> 00:58:00.342
Everything's gonna be okay.

561
00:58:42.152 --> 00:58:45.086
- I'm glad you're taking care
of yourself.

562
00:59:10.079 --> 00:59:12.313
- Did you go for another drive
tonight?

563
00:59:14.217 --> 00:59:15.449
- Mm-hmm.

564
00:59:20.990 --> 00:59:22.958
- I need to know if you're okay.

565
00:59:24.862 --> 00:59:29.097
- It's been stressful,
but I feel better.

566
00:59:35.271 --> 00:59:37.739
- I need you here with us, Evan.

567
00:59:47.617 --> 00:59:48.916
- I'm here.

568
01:00:15.713 --> 01:00:17.313
Honey...

569
01:00:17.764 --> 01:00:21.115
I thought you told her
not to watch TV with the baby.

570
01:00:21.585 --> 01:00:23.784
- I did. Sorry.

571
01:00:28.559 --> 01:00:31.110
: <i>In other news,</i>
<i>shock and horror today</i>

572
01:00:31.210 --> 01:00:32.878
<i>at the Pine Street Development,</i>

573
01:00:32.978 --> 01:00:35.213
<i>abandoned and sitting empty</i>
<i>since 2008.</i>

574
01:00:35.313 --> 01:00:37.550
<i>A woman walking her dog</i>
<i>in the area</i>

575
01:00:37.650 --> 01:00:39.385
<i>was stunned</i>
<i>to discover the body</i>

576
01:00:39.485 --> 01:00:41.788
<i>of an adult male buried</i>
<i>amidst the deserted property.</i>

577
01:00:41.887 --> 01:00:43.684
: Marie, please,
don't watch TV with Andrew.

578
01:00:43.784 --> 01:00:45.262
: <i>Three victims</i>
<i>have been confirmed,</i>

579
01:00:45.362 --> 01:00:46.880
<i>but police believe</i>
<i>there may be more.</i>

580
01:00:46.980 --> 01:00:48.809
- I'm sorry.
It won't happen again.

581
01:00:51.614 --> 01:00:53.815
- Okay. Thank you.

582
01:01:12.969 --> 01:01:14.335
- It's my fault.

583
01:01:20.811 --> 01:01:22.577
I hated him.

584
01:01:23.547 --> 01:01:25.347
- It's not your fault, Ray.

585
01:01:26.684 --> 01:01:29.083
- I hated him,
but I didn't want him dead.

586
01:01:29.652 --> 01:01:32.572
- Ray, I promise things will
get better with time.

587
01:01:32.672 --> 01:01:34.188
- How the fuck do you know?

588
01:01:35.224 --> 01:01:36.590
- I know.

589
01:01:42.498 --> 01:01:45.251
Kelly, let's talk about this.

590
01:01:45.351 --> 01:01:47.936
How you feel about
what happened to your uncle?

591
01:02:03.152 --> 01:02:04.885
- He wasn't the best dad,

592
01:02:05.989 --> 01:02:08.623
but he was my dad,
and he was changing.

593
01:02:09.492 --> 01:02:11.492
He really was, Mr. Cole.

594
01:02:15.898 --> 01:02:17.884
Whoever did this
took away my only chance

595
01:02:17.983 --> 01:02:18.985
to ever really know him.

596
01:02:19.085 --> 01:02:20.485
You know, the real him.

597
01:02:20.585 --> 01:02:24.271
- Chris, I know this is hard...

598
01:02:25.775 --> 01:02:28.610
But do you really think he was
gonna be able to stay sober?

599
01:02:29.246 --> 01:02:31.612
I'm sorry for the pain
that you're going through.

600
01:02:32.916 --> 01:02:35.501
I know it's almost impossible
to find any glimmer of hope

601
01:02:35.601 --> 01:02:37.152
in these moments, but...

602
01:02:38.121 --> 01:02:40.739
Don't you think that this is
maybe a blessing in disguise

603
01:02:40.840 --> 01:02:42.157
for you and your mom?

604
01:02:43.193 --> 01:02:44.391
- How could you even say that?

605
01:02:48.297 --> 01:02:50.664
- I've known many men
just like your father.

606
01:02:51.635 --> 01:02:54.469
My father was just like him,

607
01:02:56.072 --> 01:02:58.940
and he did to me the same things
your father was doing to you.

608
01:03:01.911 --> 01:03:03.711
He was never gonna change.

609
01:03:04.414 --> 01:03:06.514
I think deep down
you know that.

610
01:03:07.416 --> 01:03:08.416
- No.

611
01:03:10.954 --> 01:03:12.952
He was spending time with me,
he was going to AA,

612
01:03:13.052 --> 01:03:14.052
he was getting help.

613
01:03:14.150 --> 01:03:15.322
- He lied to you.

614
01:03:16.659 --> 01:03:18.177
Don't you think
it's a bit convenient

615
01:03:18.277 --> 01:03:19.579
that he shows up clean and sober

616
01:03:19.679 --> 01:03:22.030
right when your mom
gets some big inheritance?

617
01:03:25.969 --> 01:03:27.869
- How did you know about
the inheritance?

618
01:03:31.974 --> 01:03:34.342
- Well, you told me
in our last session.

619
01:03:35.311 --> 01:03:36.644
Don't you remember?

620
01:03:37.648 --> 01:03:38.648
- No.

621
01:03:39.449 --> 01:03:40.849
I don't remember that.

622
01:03:42.786 --> 01:03:44.436
- Well, I can understand that.

623
01:03:44.536 --> 01:03:47.106
Periods of high stress
can affect memory.

624
01:03:47.206 --> 01:03:48.923
It's quite common, actually.

625
01:03:51.427 --> 01:03:54.480
- Yeah, okay, sure.
You're probably right.

626
01:03:54.579 --> 01:03:55.597
- Chris.

627
01:03:56.967 --> 01:03:58.751
We're not finished talking
about this.

628
01:03:58.851 --> 01:04:01.570
- Uh, I'll see you.
I'll see you later, Mr. C.

629
01:04:32.902 --> 01:04:36.036
- Good afternoon, ma'am,
I'm Detective Overstreet.

630
01:04:36.806 --> 01:04:38.423
Is this Evan Cole's residence?

631
01:04:38.523 --> 01:04:41.527
- Yes.
- And you're Mrs. Cole?

632
01:04:41.626 --> 01:04:43.945
- Yes. What's this about?

633
01:04:44.581 --> 01:04:47.333
- Well, I just need to speak
with your husband, Mrs. Cole.

634
01:04:47.432 --> 01:04:48.550
Is he home?

635
01:04:51.088 --> 01:04:53.387
- No, but he should be shortly.

636
01:04:54.824 --> 01:04:56.123
- I can wait.

637
01:05:01.197 --> 01:05:02.329
Mr. Cole,

638
01:05:03.666 --> 01:05:05.851
I'm sure you've heard by now
about the burial site

639
01:05:05.952 --> 01:05:08.903
that was uncovered over near
the Pine Street Development.

640
01:05:09.438 --> 01:05:10.672
- I heard.

641
01:05:12.009 --> 01:05:13.340
It's horrible.

642
01:05:14.878 --> 01:05:17.778
- Did you know all three men
had one thing in common?

643
01:05:20.217 --> 01:05:23.985
They all have relatives that
are students at your school.

644
01:05:25.922 --> 01:05:27.322
In fact...

645
01:05:29.393 --> 01:05:33.460
I believe you see all
of the students in question.

646
01:05:35.032 --> 01:05:36.597
- Yes, of course.

647
01:05:38.068 --> 01:05:39.068
They're...

648
01:05:40.871 --> 01:05:43.838
they're very upset.
It's very hard on them.

649
01:05:46.309 --> 01:05:48.643
I'm sure you know, Detective...?

650
01:05:51.248 --> 01:05:52.514
- Overstreet.

651
01:05:53.483 --> 01:05:55.150
- ...Overstreet.

652
01:05:57.454 --> 01:05:59.688
All my clients are children
at risk.

653
01:06:00.389 --> 01:06:03.775
Many of them have problematic
family lives--

654
01:06:03.876 --> 01:06:07.795
drug abuse,
criminality, mental illness.

655
01:06:08.798 --> 01:06:12.032
Often their family members
are at risk themselves.

656
01:06:12.668 --> 01:06:14.719
And our school
is a regional high school,

657
01:06:14.820 --> 01:06:16.521
with over 5000 students, so...

658
01:06:16.621 --> 01:06:18.556
- Yeah, well, uh...

659
01:06:18.657 --> 01:06:22.344
We have several options that
we're looking into right now.

660
01:06:23.746 --> 01:06:25.425
How long have you been
a counselor there?

661
01:06:25.525 --> 01:06:28.067
- Social worker.
- Oh...

662
01:06:28.166 --> 01:06:29.516
- Little over a year.

663
01:06:31.688 --> 01:06:34.688
Are you saying that you think that
I might have something to do with this?

664
01:06:36.492 --> 01:06:38.726
- It raises some red flags.

665
01:06:42.599 --> 01:06:44.865
But I'm just covering
all my bases.

666
01:06:45.335 --> 01:06:46.818
- Of course.
- You understand.

667
01:06:46.918 --> 01:06:48.536
- We've all got a job to do.

668
01:06:49.539 --> 01:06:50.605
- Mmm.

669
01:06:51.842 --> 01:06:53.641
Social...

670
01:06:53.826 --> 01:06:55.710
Now, where were you
working before?

671
01:06:57.114 --> 01:07:00.014
- I'm happy to send my
employment record if you like.

672
01:07:04.521 --> 01:07:07.121
- Uh... okay.

673
01:07:10.659 --> 01:07:11.960
Thank you.

674
01:07:14.398 --> 01:07:15.697
And, uh...

675
01:07:19.168 --> 01:07:20.869
Here's my card.

676
01:07:21.704 --> 01:07:24.072
Any information
will be helpful.

677
01:07:25.375 --> 01:07:26.875
I'll show myself out.

678
01:07:44.094 --> 01:07:45.960
Uh, Mrs. Cole...

679
01:07:48.597 --> 01:07:52.117
Has your husband had any late night
absences that you've noticed?

680
01:07:52.217 --> 01:07:54.119
: Of course not, officer.

681
01:07:54.219 --> 01:07:58.239
My son is a very dedicated
father and husband.

682
01:08:01.043 --> 01:08:02.409
- Mrs. Cole?

683
01:08:05.382 --> 01:08:06.382
- No.

684
01:08:07.583 --> 01:08:08.916
Nothing like that.

685
01:08:15.025 --> 01:08:19.159
- Are you a heavy sleeper,
Mrs. Cole?

686
01:08:25.635 --> 01:08:28.770
Excuse me, Detective.

687
01:08:30.372 --> 01:08:32.891
- Oh, no, no.
Here you go, Mom.

688
01:08:32.992 --> 01:08:35.810
- Thank you, Marie. Shh, shh.

689
01:08:44.820 --> 01:08:46.054
- Thank you.

690
01:08:54.230 --> 01:08:55.497
- Don't.

691
01:08:58.400 --> 01:08:59.533
- What is it?

692
01:09:01.137 --> 01:09:02.537
- Nothing.

693
01:09:04.975 --> 01:09:06.306
It's nothing.

694
01:09:26.095 --> 01:09:29.063
Oh, hello, Detective.
Evan's still at work.

695
01:09:30.500 --> 01:09:33.001
- I'm not here to see
Mr. Cole, ma'am.

696
01:09:40.010 --> 01:09:41.842
- What is this about?

697
01:09:44.014 --> 01:09:45.246
- Um...

698
01:09:48.051 --> 01:09:50.551
Do you know Chris Wells?

699
01:09:52.354 --> 01:09:54.087
- He's one of Evan's patients.

700
01:09:55.158 --> 01:09:57.926
- Did your husband ever see him
outside of his office?

701
01:09:59.729 --> 01:10:00.729
- No.

702
01:10:04.134 --> 01:10:05.567
- Are you sure?

703
01:10:07.136 --> 01:10:09.203
- What are you trying to say,
Detective?

704
01:10:13.676 --> 01:10:15.243
- How long...

705
01:10:17.146 --> 01:10:18.445
have you...

706
01:10:19.381 --> 01:10:21.282
known your husband?

707
01:10:21.751 --> 01:10:23.217
- Three years. Why?

708
01:10:26.488 --> 01:10:28.756
- You know where he lived
before you met?

709
01:10:31.060 --> 01:10:32.894
- Uh, near the desert.

710
01:10:35.231 --> 01:10:37.783
I really don't see why
this matters at all, Detective.

711
01:10:37.882 --> 01:10:40.685
- Uh, well, a year
after he left Hemet,

712
01:10:40.786 --> 01:10:42.688
police uncovered a site

713
01:10:42.787 --> 01:10:45.073
not unlike the Pine Street
Development.

714
01:10:47.077 --> 01:10:49.310
- What does that have to do
with anything?

715
01:10:51.514 --> 01:10:52.980
- Maybe nothing,

716
01:10:53.550 --> 01:10:55.333
but it's my job
to see connections,

717
01:10:55.434 --> 01:10:58.953
and right now, I have to say,
I'm beginning to see something.

718
01:11:06.395 --> 01:11:08.695
- Do you know
where your husband was

719
01:11:09.399 --> 01:11:13.501
the night of Thursday,
March 26th?

720
01:11:18.307 --> 01:11:22.143
- I do, actually. He was
at the hospital with me.

721
01:11:22.878 --> 01:11:24.529
Our son was running
a high fever,

722
01:11:24.630 --> 01:11:26.180
and we took him into the E.R.

723
01:11:30.252 --> 01:11:31.653
- Uh...

724
01:11:35.658 --> 01:11:38.077
Now, this camera is
at the corner

725
01:11:38.176 --> 01:11:40.028
of Third and MacDonald.

726
01:11:40.963 --> 01:11:43.530
Now, is this on the way
to the hospital from here?

727
01:11:44.134 --> 01:11:45.251
'Cause I have to admit,

728
01:11:45.350 --> 01:11:47.167
I don't know
this neighborhood very well.

729
01:11:58.515 --> 01:12:00.847
- Do you have kids, Detective?

730
01:12:01.917 --> 01:12:03.518
- Never had the urge.

731
01:12:07.090 --> 01:12:10.190
- When you have a baby,
everything changes.

732
01:12:11.094 --> 01:12:12.859
But not like everyone says.

733
01:12:13.430 --> 01:12:15.363
It's like you're going crazy.

734
01:12:15.864 --> 01:12:18.550
You never sleep.
The baby cries all the time.

735
01:12:18.649 --> 01:12:21.836
Every little thing feels
like a crisis.

736
01:12:23.105 --> 01:12:25.323
I can't even describe to you
what it feels like

737
01:12:25.423 --> 01:12:28.293
to be filled with love and
total panic at the same time.

738
01:12:28.394 --> 01:12:31.829
- Yeah, well,
I'm sure it's very
difficult, Mrs. Cole, but--

739
01:12:31.930 --> 01:12:34.466
- My husband deals with people
in crisis every day,

740
01:12:34.565 --> 01:12:37.918
and he was coming home and
feeling like he was in crisis.

741
01:12:39.689 --> 01:12:42.173
He took drives, alone at night,

742
01:12:42.274 --> 01:12:44.257
for some space and peace,
and do you know what?

743
01:12:44.894 --> 01:12:46.894
I totally understand.

744
01:12:47.697 --> 01:12:49.280
And I gave him that space,

745
01:12:49.381 --> 01:12:51.466
and trusted
that he would come home.

746
01:12:51.900 --> 01:12:53.568
And he did.

747
01:12:56.139 --> 01:12:57.872
He always did.

748
01:13:06.082 --> 01:13:07.114
- Hmm.

749
01:13:12.721 --> 01:13:15.555
Give me a call if you think
of anything else...

750
01:13:17.193 --> 01:13:19.060
or you just want to talk.

751
01:13:20.829 --> 01:13:22.480
Because from where
I'm standing,

752
01:13:22.581 --> 01:13:24.431
it's just a matter
of time.

753
01:13:28.570 --> 01:13:29.970
- Thank you, Detective.

754
01:13:31.541 --> 01:13:33.173
I'll keep that in mind.

755
01:13:38.948 --> 01:13:41.181
That detective came over again.

756
01:13:42.085 --> 01:13:44.519
- Oh, yeah? What'd he want?

757
01:13:46.122 --> 01:13:48.122
- Asked me a bunch of questions.

758
01:13:50.092 --> 01:13:52.527
About where you lived
before you moved here.

759
01:13:55.465 --> 01:13:57.315
And he also asked me
where you were

760
01:13:57.416 --> 01:13:59.266
the night we took Andrew
to the E.R.

761
01:14:04.573 --> 01:14:07.608
- Really? What'd you tell him?

762
01:14:08.310 --> 01:14:10.511
- That we were at the hospital,
of course.

763
01:14:13.048 --> 01:14:15.716
- Well, hopefully he won't be back
around to bother you again.

764
01:14:21.123 --> 01:14:22.556
- Hopefully.

765
01:14:38.507 --> 01:14:40.408
- I'll tell her to turn it off.

766
01:14:44.514 --> 01:14:45.713
: Mom.

767
01:14:45.863 --> 01:14:47.501
<i>: Police are trying</i>
<i>to find a connection</i>

768
01:14:47.600 --> 01:14:48.719
<i>between Caroline Herrington,</i>

769
01:14:48.819 --> 01:14:50.935
<i>a nurse in pediatric care</i>
<i>at Temescal Hospital,</i>

770
01:14:51.036 --> 01:14:53.404
<i>who was found on a gurney</i>
<i>outside the morgue,</i>

771
01:14:53.505 --> 01:14:55.106
<i>having been</i>
<i>brutally murdered.</i>

772
01:14:55.207 --> 01:14:57.475
<i>It seems the killing occurred</i>
<i>in the staff locker room</i>

773
01:14:57.576 --> 01:15:01.529
<i>as Miss Harrington was finishing</i>
<i>her night shift. What a week.</i>

774
01:15:01.965 --> 01:15:04.750
<i>Well, after that, I sure could</i>
<i>use some good news.</i>

775
01:15:04.850 --> 01:15:06.289
<i>Over to Brian with--</i>
- Turn it off.

776
01:15:06.970 --> 01:15:08.654
Of course, dear.
: <i>Thanks, Diane.</i>

777
01:15:08.753 --> 01:15:10.922
<i>Sunny skies and 72</i>
<i>all weekend.</i>

778
01:15:11.023 --> 01:15:12.506
<i>It's a good one</i>
<i>to pack up the--</i>

779
01:15:20.949 --> 01:15:24.435
: Mr. C?
Come out here, Mr. C!

780
01:15:24.536 --> 01:15:27.421
- What is it?
- It's Chris Wells.

781
01:15:28.157 --> 01:15:29.524
I'll take care of it.

782
01:15:30.527 --> 01:15:32.310
It's okay. I got it.

783
01:15:32.411 --> 01:15:33.694
- Mr. C!

784
01:15:37.065 --> 01:15:40.100
Mr. C!
- Chris.

785
01:15:41.003 --> 01:15:43.255
Hey. You all right?

786
01:15:43.354 --> 01:15:45.305
- I know it was you.

787
01:15:46.175 --> 01:15:47.707
- What was me, buddy?

788
01:15:48.377 --> 01:15:50.211
- I know you killed my dad.

789
01:15:50.813 --> 01:15:53.030
- Chris, you're drunk.

790
01:15:53.131 --> 01:15:55.815
- I never told you
about the money. I know it.

791
01:15:56.985 --> 01:15:59.671
Which means he told you.
- Calm down.

792
01:15:59.770 --> 01:16:01.922
Let me make you some coffee,
and we'll talk.

793
01:16:02.824 --> 01:16:04.725
- I don't think so, Mr. C.

794
01:16:08.331 --> 01:16:09.796
Tell me the truth.

795
01:16:10.699 --> 01:16:12.899
- I would never do anything
to hurt you.

796
01:16:14.503 --> 01:16:16.604
You're like a son to me, Chris.

797
01:16:17.273 --> 01:16:18.939
I just want the best for you.

798
01:16:21.578 --> 01:16:22.743
- Evan.

799
01:16:25.448 --> 01:16:27.032
- It's okay, Lauren.

800
01:16:27.131 --> 01:16:28.849
Take Andrew back to his room.

801
01:16:30.686 --> 01:16:31.786
Lauren.

802
01:16:41.396 --> 01:16:42.630
It's okay.

803
01:16:44.399 --> 01:16:47.635
It's okay, Chris.
You'll be all right. Shh.

804
01:16:49.305 --> 01:16:52.206
Shh. You'll be okay.
It's all right.

805
01:16:53.909 --> 01:16:54.909
Shh.

806
01:16:57.113 --> 01:16:59.664
Shh. It's okay.

807
01:16:59.765 --> 01:17:00.765
Shh.

808
01:17:04.753 --> 01:17:05.753
Shh.

809
01:17:13.997 --> 01:17:15.529
You're gonna be okay.

810
01:17:19.668 --> 01:17:23.570
Come on, let me take you home.
You sleep this off.

811
01:17:24.774 --> 01:17:26.039
- Don't touch me!

812
01:17:38.921 --> 01:17:40.320
- I'm sorry about that.

813
01:17:41.189 --> 01:17:42.689
He's confused...

814
01:17:43.826 --> 01:17:45.326
traumatized.

815
01:17:59.475 --> 01:18:01.676
I got it. Sleep.

816
01:18:11.720 --> 01:18:14.087
I like to think that
I'm a good man, Andrew.

817
01:18:15.390 --> 01:18:17.425
That I help people.

818
01:18:19.662 --> 01:18:22.229
<i>But sometimes life</i>
<i>backs you into a corner,</i>

819
01:18:23.466 --> 01:18:26.466
<i>and you just don't have</i>
<i>any choice. You know?</i>

820
01:18:28.470 --> 01:18:31.288
<i>No, you don't,</i>
<i>do you, pal?</i>

821
01:18:31.389 --> 01:18:32.806
<i>Not yet.</i>

822
01:18:34.976 --> 01:18:38.145
<i>But no matter what, I love you.</i>

823
01:18:39.649 --> 01:18:42.382
<i>I'll do whatever it takes</i>
<i>to keep us together.</i>

824
01:21:35.824 --> 01:21:37.257
- He's hungry.

825
01:21:40.496 --> 01:21:41.662
Here you go.

826
01:21:48.738 --> 01:21:51.572
I think our Evan
is in a tough spot, dear.

827
01:21:52.440 --> 01:21:53.740
Don't you?

828
01:21:54.777 --> 01:21:57.978
It wasn't easy for him
as a boy.

829
01:21:59.381 --> 01:22:01.282
He was... different.

830
01:22:02.952 --> 01:22:05.152
But Evan was a good boy.

831
01:22:07.023 --> 01:22:08.788
And he's a good man.

832
01:22:13.930 --> 01:22:15.846
He learned the hard way

833
01:22:15.947 --> 01:22:19.466
that children
need to be protected...

834
01:22:20.536 --> 01:22:24.671
that families
need to be protected.

835
01:22:35.417 --> 01:22:37.952
But now you have a family
of your own to protect.

836
01:22:41.890 --> 01:22:43.724
Sometimes...

837
01:22:44.393 --> 01:22:47.560
the cost of that
protection...

838
01:22:48.997 --> 01:22:50.663
...can be a little high.

839
01:22:59.074 --> 01:23:01.760
It must have been hard
for you too,

840
01:23:01.859 --> 01:23:04.677
as a little girl
with no family.

841
01:23:06.481 --> 01:23:09.582
I can't imagine
what you went through.

842
01:23:13.122 --> 01:23:14.755
- It was horrible...

843
01:23:16.292 --> 01:23:17.992
the things I had to do.

844
01:23:22.998 --> 01:23:26.367
- Thank goodness Andrew will
never have to go through that.

845
01:23:30.972 --> 01:23:34.375
We do everything we can
for our sons.

846
01:23:35.711 --> 01:23:37.344
Don't we, dear?

847
01:23:54.162 --> 01:23:55.346
- Hi, sweetheart.

848
01:23:55.447 --> 01:23:58.015
<i>Hey, babe.</i>
<i>Can you do me a favor?</i>

849
01:23:58.115 --> 01:23:59.184
- Of course.

850
01:23:59.283 --> 01:24:01.086
<i>Can you watch Andrew</i>
<i>after school?</i>

851
01:24:01.185 --> 01:24:02.921
- Oh. Uh...

852
01:24:03.020 --> 01:24:04.956
<i>I need to get out</i>
<i>of the house for a few hours.</i>

853
01:24:05.055 --> 01:24:06.591
<i>Go get my nails done,</i>

854
01:24:06.690 --> 01:24:08.859
<i>go to the grocery store--</i>
<i>I don't know.</i>

855
01:24:08.960 --> 01:24:11.029
<i>Anything that doesn't involve</i>
<i>getting puked on.</i>

856
01:24:11.128 --> 01:24:13.864
- Sure. Of course
I'll watch him.

857
01:24:13.965 --> 01:24:15.381
<i>Thank you, sweetheart.</i>

858
01:24:16.886 --> 01:24:18.786
I'll be home before bedtime.

859
01:24:46.948 --> 01:24:49.515
It's Lauren, Mrs. Cole.

860
01:24:51.787 --> 01:24:52.787
Hi.

861
01:24:55.690 --> 01:24:58.826
Listen, I heard what you said
last night.

862
01:25:00.429 --> 01:25:01.828
I believe you.

863
01:25:02.698 --> 01:25:04.481
<i>Um, I'm afraid.</i>

864
01:25:04.582 --> 01:25:08.101
<i>I'm afraid for Andrew,</i>
<i>and I need to do something.</i>

865
01:25:09.738 --> 01:25:10.738
<i>Yes.</i>

866
01:25:12.574 --> 01:25:15.007
<i>Thank you. See you there.</i>

867
01:25:25.453 --> 01:25:27.520
- Did Lauren leave already?

868
01:25:28.157 --> 01:25:30.023
- She said
she was going shopping.

869
01:25:31.292 --> 01:25:33.627
- Yeah.
She said she needed time.

870
01:25:34.997 --> 01:25:36.563
- And you believe her?

871
01:25:40.136 --> 01:25:41.667
- Lauren would never...

872
01:25:42.637 --> 01:25:44.337
She needs this family.

873
01:25:48.109 --> 01:25:49.643
- What about the boy?

874
01:28:09.318 --> 01:28:10.350
: Mrs. Cole?

875
01:28:18.127 --> 01:28:19.826
Do you really believe me?

876
01:28:21.796 --> 01:28:23.229
- He did it, Chris.

877
01:28:24.332 --> 01:28:26.632
But the thing
that makes it so sad,

878
01:28:27.069 --> 01:28:28.835
is that he did it for you.

879
01:28:32.975 --> 01:28:34.841
I'm really sorry, Chris.

880
01:29:20.956 --> 01:29:22.355
Lauren.

881
01:29:33.868 --> 01:29:37.788
<i>In a shocking suicide confession
posted to Facebook late last night,</i>

882
01:29:37.889 --> 01:29:39.990
<i>Christopher Wells,</i>
<i>honor student,</i>

883
01:29:40.091 --> 01:29:42.092
<i>just awarded a full</i>
<i>scholarship to Stanford,</i>

884
01:29:42.193 --> 01:29:46.497
<i>has confessed to the three "Deadbeat</i>
<i>Dad" murders uncovered here last week.</i>

885
01:29:46.596 --> 01:29:49.367
<i>The revelation has sent
shockwaves through the community,</i>

886
01:29:49.466 --> 01:29:51.668
<i>not only because</i>
<i>of the brutality</i>

887
01:29:51.769 --> 01:29:55.605
<i>of the murders themselves,</i>
<i>but because of the student's youth
and academic promise.</i>

888
01:29:55.706 --> 01:29:58.309
<i>Fellow students are organizing</i>
<i>a candlelight vigil,</i>

889
01:29:58.408 --> 01:30:00.377
<i>but sources say</i>
<i>there are mixed feelings</i>

890
01:30:00.478 --> 01:30:01.679
<i>in the school halls.</i>

891
01:30:01.779 --> 01:30:03.381
<i>Detective John Overstreet...</i>

892
01:30:03.480 --> 01:30:05.064
: Hello, Detective.

893
01:30:05.900 --> 01:30:07.667
- You know,
it's a different world.

894
01:30:09.570 --> 01:30:11.837
These kids put everything
on the Internet.

895
01:30:16.444 --> 01:30:19.945
You have any idea how he could have
gotten access to your files?

896
01:30:22.518 --> 01:30:24.484
- I let him get too close.

897
01:30:26.421 --> 01:30:29.373
Let him, uh,
hang in my office

898
01:30:29.474 --> 01:30:31.394
when he was trying to get away
from everything.

899
01:30:32.560 --> 01:30:34.127
Maybe I shouldn't have.

900
01:30:37.565 --> 01:30:39.698
- Well... with the, uh...

901
01:30:40.536 --> 01:30:44.371
confession and the, uh, suicide
with the victim's own weapon,

902
01:30:46.108 --> 01:30:48.108
not much else to look into.

903
01:30:50.612 --> 01:30:53.145
And I'm sorry for your loss,
Mr. Cole.

904
01:30:56.118 --> 01:30:57.818
- Thank you, Detective.

905
01:31:07.729 --> 01:31:09.695
- Well, I will, uh...

906
01:31:11.466 --> 01:31:13.065
I'll show myself out.

907
01:31:17.171 --> 01:31:18.722
- Goodbye, Detective.

908
01:31:18.823 --> 01:31:21.574
Thank you so much
for stopping by.

909
01:31:40.496 --> 01:31:41.927
Pancakes?

910
01:32:06.188 --> 01:32:09.221
